# Scanner laws (full brief: AGENTS.md)

- PUBLIC engine on six registries: the `ScanReport` wire is
  additive-only forever; score semantic changes bump `score_contract`;
  public enums stay `#[non_exhaustive]`.
- "No QR found" is `Ok` with empty detections — `Err` = `QRS-001..005`
  only (stable registry, never reused).
- Determinism: `budget_ms: None` must stay strictly reproducible —
  no RNG, no clocks in the scan path.
- Zero `unwrap`/`expect`/`panic!` in production (lint-denied); engine
  panics degrade to no-score at the boundary, never a crash.
- Decoded text is attacker-controlled — strip terminal controls on any
  human echo; colour only via the CLI's term.rs seam.
- Gates: `cargo nextest run --workspace` + doc tests + clippy
  all-features -D warnings + `scripts/check-type-parity.py` +
  `cargo +1.88 check --locked` + `xtask corpus-report`.
- Release = bump workspace + `xtask sync-version` (9 surfaces) + tag;
  RELEASING.md is the ritual. Downstream repos pin this version as
  "the judge" — score honesty is a contract.
- Commits: `type(scope): lowercase` + `Co-Authored-By: Nika 🦋
  <nika@supernovae.studio>`.
